WEBVTT

00:23.523 --> 00:24.941
This is...

00:25.025 --> 00:26.317
Yes.

00:26.401 --> 00:27.694
It's the hole Richeh made.

00:27.777 --> 00:28.778
DRAGON'S MAZE

00:28.862 --> 00:30.030
How many times has it been?

00:30.113 --> 00:32.073
I've stopped counting.

00:32.157 --> 00:35.827
Let's hide somewhere covered for now.

00:35.910 --> 00:38.079
It's gotten cold too.

00:58.850 --> 01:01.186
You dropped this.

01:05.482 --> 01:07.525
Oh, thanks.

01:09.694 --> 01:12.030
Um, are you okay?

01:15.200 --> 01:17.202
Of course you're not.

01:17.285 --> 01:19.621
I'm sorry. It's my fault.

01:22.540 --> 01:23.374
Well--

01:23.458 --> 01:26.336
Oh, your cloak! Wear this!
You'll freeze without one!

01:26.419 --> 01:28.213
And I'll stick close to you!

01:37.222 --> 01:41.184
I feel safe when I wear that.

01:43.228 --> 01:47.023
When I have it on, no one can tell
even if I'm scared and shaking.

01:47.607 --> 01:50.235
At least on the outside,
I can stay a witch.

01:50.318 --> 01:51.653
It gives me courage.

01:52.153 --> 01:55.073
So for now, I want you to wear it, Tetia.

01:55.573 --> 01:58.535
Better off on you
than on someone useless like me.

02:01.121 --> 02:02.288
Whoa!

02:02.372 --> 02:03.665
Huh? Wait... What?!

02:05.917 --> 02:07.544
What are you doing?

02:09.879 --> 02:12.006
Oh, it's warm.

02:12.632 --> 02:13.508
A cloud?

02:14.134 --> 02:15.176
I'm sorry!

02:15.260 --> 02:17.595
For giving you an accusatory look, Coco.

02:17.679 --> 02:18.930
What?

02:22.517 --> 02:24.978
It's fine! You're right anyway.

02:25.061 --> 02:28.189
And thank you for not saying anything.

02:29.107 --> 02:31.276
But I let it show.

02:31.359 --> 02:35.155
I took my fear out on you, Coco.

02:35.655 --> 02:37.365
I'm senior to you.

02:37.448 --> 02:40.076
I should be looking out for you.

02:43.913 --> 02:45.456
You are looking after me!

02:45.540 --> 02:49.335
Your magic is so warm!
I'm actually relaxed in this situation!

02:49.419 --> 02:51.337
Incredible! Magic is amazing!

02:53.047 --> 02:56.342
This spell is my original.

02:56.926 --> 03:00.930
When I was little,
I wanted to nap on a cloud.

03:01.014 --> 03:02.849
I've been experimenting ever since.

03:02.932 --> 03:04.934
It's far from perfected though.

03:05.435 --> 03:08.479
When it's done, I want to submit it
for communal magic review

03:08.563 --> 03:10.815
so everyone can use it.

03:11.316 --> 03:15.737
It may not be helpful,
but it's an important dream to me.

03:15.820 --> 03:19.407
So you should wear your cloak, Coco.

03:19.490 --> 03:22.327
We'll take off our apprentice cloaks
when we make it back

03:22.410 --> 03:25.246
and we all become witches together.

03:25.872 --> 03:26.998
Okay?

03:30.293 --> 03:31.294
Yeah!

03:34.923 --> 03:36.382
- If...
- Whoa!

03:36.466 --> 03:40.220
If you want to ride it, you'll have to
create something with more substance.

03:40.303 --> 03:41.846
It's freezing out here.

03:42.347 --> 03:43.598
Let me in too.

03:43.681 --> 03:45.266
If you want people to fly in it,

03:45.350 --> 03:47.727
just use a sub that looks like a cloud.

03:47.810 --> 03:48.645
Like cotton.

03:48.728 --> 03:51.231
Then that's just a regular blanket.

03:51.314 --> 03:55.151
Dreams are nice and all,
but let's get back to reality.

03:55.902 --> 03:58.780
Like how we're going to get out of here.

03:59.697 --> 04:02.784
The fact that we keep running
and ending up back in the same place

04:02.867 --> 04:06.412
tells me the entire area is under a spell.

04:06.496 --> 04:08.915
Whatever kind of forbidden magic it is,

04:08.998 --> 04:11.668
if it's magic,
there should be a seal somewhere.

04:12.377 --> 04:14.254
First, we need to find it--

04:14.337 --> 04:15.755
- Um...
- Huh?

04:17.090 --> 04:21.344
I may have seen the seal. Maybe?

04:22.720 --> 04:24.305
You're right.

04:24.389 --> 04:25.223
Toward the top.

04:27.183 --> 04:28.935
Yep. That's a seal.

04:29.018 --> 04:30.311
Huh?

04:30.395 --> 04:33.273
Does the dragon seem like
it's gotten bigger?

04:33.356 --> 04:35.692
Maybe we're shrinking.

04:35.775 --> 04:37.819
- Along with the space.
- What?

04:37.902 --> 04:39.153
Either way,

04:39.237 --> 04:42.949
if the dragon is protecting the seal,
we have to defeat it.

04:43.032 --> 04:44.951
- Guess it's fire magic--
- Wait.

04:46.119 --> 04:49.914
The fire magic didn't really work earlier.

04:50.915 --> 04:53.126
- What?
- No, I mean...

04:53.793 --> 04:56.963
It flinched but didn't seem
to take much damage.

04:57.463 --> 05:01.509
So I don't think we'll beat it with fire.

05:03.219 --> 05:05.638
Then what are you suggesting?

05:05.722 --> 05:06.889
We don't defeat it.

05:12.979 --> 05:15.940
Are you still hung up on
what I said earlier?

05:16.024 --> 05:17.150
No, no.

05:17.233 --> 05:20.278
I only thought of it
because of you and Tetia.

05:20.361 --> 05:21.529
Huh?

05:22.238 --> 05:23.573
I have a plan.

05:24.073 --> 05:26.284
I don't know if it'll work,

05:26.367 --> 05:27.744
but I want to try it.

05:35.626 --> 05:36.794
Is this...

05:36.878 --> 05:38.338
Yes!

05:38.421 --> 05:41.549
Operation Let's-Finish-Tetia's-Dream!

05:43.301 --> 05:44.552
What do you mean?

05:44.635 --> 05:46.804
Well, you know how it's cold here?

05:46.888 --> 05:49.849
But Tetia's cloud was warm
and comforting.

05:49.932 --> 05:53.478
So if we made a cloud blanket
for the dragon, too,

05:53.561 --> 05:55.355
it won't want to move,

05:55.438 --> 05:57.315
and maybe it won't attack us.

05:57.398 --> 05:58.524
But isn't that...

05:58.608 --> 05:59.817
True.

06:00.610 --> 06:03.488
No one can resist the power
of a comfy blanket.

06:03.571 --> 06:05.448
Maybe not even the dragon.

06:05.531 --> 06:06.949
I know, right?

06:07.033 --> 06:08.451
Seriously?

06:08.534 --> 06:10.036
But that's...

06:11.954 --> 06:14.624
Wait, hold on.
Let me organize my thoughts.

06:15.124 --> 06:17.877
It's true that for humans...

06:20.838 --> 06:23.633
Coco, what's wrong?

06:23.716 --> 06:26.010
Oh, no, it's nothing.

06:26.094 --> 06:29.013
I was just wondering if the dragon's okay.

06:30.890 --> 06:32.141
The dragon?

06:32.225 --> 06:35.269
Earlier, when we were running, it, um,

06:35.353 --> 06:38.648
went "bam"!
Face-first, straight into a pillar.

06:38.731 --> 06:41.609
At the time,
I was too desperate and scared,

06:42.110 --> 06:45.655
but thinking back,
it must have really hurt.

06:46.906 --> 06:48.699
So, um,

06:48.783 --> 06:50.785
what I'm trying to say is,

06:51.369 --> 06:54.914
that's why
I really wanted to try this plan!

06:58.251 --> 07:02.839
Master said the magic that wasn't banned

07:02.922 --> 07:05.591
still exists to make people happy.

07:06.300 --> 07:07.427
And so

07:07.510 --> 07:10.263
he wanted me to learn kinder magic.

07:11.013 --> 07:15.017
If this works, no one will get hurt.

07:15.726 --> 07:18.980
Not us, and not that dragon either.

07:22.859 --> 07:23.901
Right!

07:23.985 --> 07:26.696
And besides, if Agott helps,

07:26.779 --> 07:29.782
I think it'll turn out even better!

07:29.866 --> 07:32.118
It seemed like you had ideas.

07:33.870 --> 07:36.956
Well, it's not like I don't...

07:37.498 --> 07:39.750
Then let's all do it together.

07:41.502 --> 07:44.755
You're the best at drawing
out of all of us, Agott.

07:45.256 --> 07:47.925
It'd be reassuring to have you with us.

07:58.561 --> 07:59.687
Well...

08:01.397 --> 08:02.690
Fine, then.

08:02.773 --> 08:04.108
- Yes!
- Yay!

08:04.192 --> 08:06.152
- Oops! Whoa...
- Hey, watch out!

08:09.530 --> 08:11.115
Thank you, Agott!

08:11.199 --> 08:14.452
I don't need thanks. Let's get planning.

08:14.535 --> 08:15.536
Okay!

08:18.706 --> 08:20.958
You want to ride on this, right, Tetia?

08:21.042 --> 08:22.084
Right!

08:22.168 --> 08:24.462
I want it to be like a fluffy bed!

08:24.962 --> 08:26.672
Something fluffy,

08:26.756 --> 08:29.050
but you can't slip through like a cloud.

08:29.133 --> 08:31.636
- Hmm...
- Something available here...

08:31.719 --> 08:35.139
And sturdy enough to hold a dragon.

08:36.224 --> 08:37.850
Torn paper!

08:37.934 --> 08:40.561
Even if we rip out all our quires,
it won't be enough.

08:40.645 --> 08:42.063
- Cloth!
- Hair...

08:42.146 --> 08:45.066
That's nowhere near enough.
And you're fine using those up?

08:48.319 --> 08:50.279
- Sand...
- Huh?

08:51.113 --> 08:52.448
How about sand?

08:53.991 --> 08:55.284
The Wall Breaker Seal!

08:55.368 --> 08:58.120
If we break the wall
and floor like we did earlier,

08:58.204 --> 08:59.539
we could make fine sand.

08:59.622 --> 09:03.292
Oh, right! Sand is soft and fluffy
and feels nice!

09:03.376 --> 09:05.419
Nice, Agott! That's our Agott!

09:05.503 --> 09:09.257
If we increase the arrows, we should
be able to create even finer particles.

09:09.340 --> 09:10.800
The smaller, the better.

09:10.883 --> 09:13.678
If it's small seals, leave it to me.

09:13.761 --> 09:15.388
Wow, that was fast!

09:15.471 --> 09:17.431
It's Richeh's specialty!

09:17.515 --> 09:19.183
Tetia, try to come up with a spell

09:19.267 --> 09:22.144
that gathers the sand in the center
without compacting it.

09:22.228 --> 09:25.523
I'll think of a spell to encase it
so it won't crumble.

09:25.606 --> 09:26.649
Understood!

09:26.732 --> 09:28.025
Um...

09:30.236 --> 09:31.696
What should I do?

09:31.779 --> 09:33.114
You stay back, Coco.

09:34.448 --> 09:36.200
I'll go along with the plan,

09:36.284 --> 09:39.912
but with your current skill,
there's no spell I can trust you with.

09:40.413 --> 09:42.790
Just don't get in the way
and it'll be fine.

09:54.218 --> 09:57.847
The circle is so clean.
How does she draw it?

10:15.740 --> 10:17.950
She traces it in the air a few times,

10:18.034 --> 10:20.411
then starts from the front.

10:21.329 --> 10:24.457
I wonder if Tetia and Richeh
draw it like that too.

10:31.505 --> 10:33.633
How did I do it?

10:34.675 --> 10:39.639
The starting point and the ending form...
I've never really thought about it before.

10:42.516 --> 10:43.809
I'll try it!

10:44.310 --> 10:47.146
I want to be able to do it
like everyone else.

10:48.981 --> 10:50.316
I'll try it!

10:51.817 --> 10:54.320
Like this and this...

11:10.711 --> 11:12.129
It's so cold.

11:12.630 --> 11:14.548
It's gotten dark.

11:14.632 --> 11:15.841
Should we light a fire?

11:15.925 --> 11:18.469
- I'm out of paper.
- Me too.

11:19.970 --> 11:21.681
It's no use.

11:21.764 --> 11:24.266
Convergence arrows
will make it too rigid...

11:24.350 --> 11:26.602
How about wrapping it in a layer of air?

11:26.686 --> 11:28.813
Not strong enough. It'll collapse.

11:29.855 --> 11:32.358
What if we shred fabric for reinforcement?

11:32.441 --> 11:34.944
Even just wrapping it, it isn't enough.

11:35.027 --> 11:36.487
Also, it'll get colder.

11:36.570 --> 11:37.405
Let's not.

11:37.488 --> 11:40.741
Hmm, there has to be a better idea...

11:40.825 --> 11:42.076
An idea...

11:42.159 --> 11:43.828
There has to be something.

11:43.911 --> 11:45.871
Something that works perfectly.

11:52.503 --> 11:53.337
I...

11:53.838 --> 11:55.297
I did it!

11:57.883 --> 12:00.469
So, why are you casting
that spell right now?

12:00.553 --> 12:02.346
- It's stable.
- Huh?

12:02.847 --> 12:06.058
The pyreball! It used to just go out!

12:06.142 --> 12:08.394
When did you learn to draw it?

12:08.477 --> 12:10.730
I was just practicing.

12:10.813 --> 12:13.023
While watching you all draw,

12:13.107 --> 12:15.943
over and over again.

12:18.279 --> 12:21.657
That's amazing. You did it, Coco!

12:22.950 --> 12:27.371
Well, anyone can get better
with enough repetition...

12:28.956 --> 12:31.542
Repetition...

12:32.376 --> 12:33.794
Repetition! That's it!

12:33.878 --> 12:34.920
- What?
- Huh?

12:41.552 --> 12:42.678
Are you ready?

12:42.762 --> 12:45.139
- Yeah.
- Ready any time.

12:46.557 --> 12:47.391
All right!

12:47.475 --> 12:48.517
Let's go!

12:59.320 --> 13:00.154
Thanks.

13:00.821 --> 13:02.740
It has gotten bigger.

13:03.240 --> 13:04.909
We need to end this quick.

13:05.493 --> 13:06.494
Richeh, go on ahead!

13:06.577 --> 13:07.411
Right.

13:44.323 --> 13:45.991
Okay. Coco!

13:46.075 --> 13:46.909
Yeah.

13:50.329 --> 13:52.456
Then give the signal to close the ring.

13:52.540 --> 13:53.415
Okay.

13:54.500 --> 13:55.417
Three...

13:55.501 --> 13:56.669
Two...

13:56.752 --> 13:57.920
- One!
- One!

14:06.053 --> 14:07.847
- Richeh, the next one!
- Right.

14:32.371 --> 14:33.455
It noticed!

14:33.539 --> 14:34.790
Let's hurry and regroup!

14:34.874 --> 14:36.041
What about their ring?

14:36.125 --> 14:37.793
All of them are activated.

14:37.877 --> 14:38.794
Good!

14:39.295 --> 14:40.546
Repetition?

14:40.629 --> 14:44.425
Yes. To keep the spell from collapsing,

14:44.508 --> 14:46.510
we have to wrap it in a repetition spell

14:46.594 --> 14:48.679
so it always goes back
to its original form.

14:49.263 --> 14:52.182
In other words,
the Wall Breaker and Billow Cluster.

14:52.266 --> 14:55.019
If we wrap this combo
in a repetition spell,

14:55.102 --> 14:57.104
we can create a cloud of sand.

14:57.187 --> 14:59.273
Considering the size of the dragon,

14:59.356 --> 15:01.108
we'll need at least five.

15:01.191 --> 15:03.235
If we sync the position and timing

15:03.319 --> 15:06.113
so all five activate as one,

15:06.196 --> 15:07.740
even if the weight makes it sink,

15:07.823 --> 15:10.951
the sand cloud will keep trying to return
to its original form,

15:11.035 --> 15:13.996
so it'll stay soft and comfy
the whole time.

15:14.955 --> 15:16.248
- Let's call--
- We'll call it...

15:25.049 --> 15:27.760
Lazy-Dragon Cushion!

15:28.719 --> 15:30.763
Vetoed. Serpent's Bed of Sand.

15:30.846 --> 15:33.265
That sounds cooler! That's our Agott!

15:33.349 --> 15:34.350
That's our Agott.

15:34.433 --> 15:37.895
Enough chatter.
Let's get through while we can.

15:43.692 --> 15:44.693
What's the matter?

15:45.194 --> 15:46.904
No, it's nothing.

15:47.738 --> 15:49.615
I was just watching.

15:50.950 --> 15:54.662
That dragon looks so happy.

15:55.663 --> 16:00.876
I think this might be the first time
I made someone happy with my magic.

16:05.214 --> 16:08.092
I didn't know it could feel so good!

16:16.266 --> 16:18.185
- Well?
- Yeah.

16:18.268 --> 16:20.145
I think this is it.

16:20.229 --> 16:21.855
What kind of spell is it?

16:21.939 --> 16:23.565
I've never seen it before.

16:24.775 --> 16:27.403
I wonder if the Master would know.

16:32.032 --> 16:33.784
Is this where they are?

16:36.036 --> 16:39.415
I don't sense anything.
Did they already move on?

16:39.498 --> 16:44.086
Huh? Wasn't this path tiled?

16:44.169 --> 16:46.463
When did they take them out?

16:47.548 --> 16:50.801
Brushbuddies are attracted
to the scent of conjuring ink.

16:52.136 --> 16:52.970
This is--

16:56.473 --> 16:57.725
- Stand back!
- Huh?

17:07.568 --> 17:10.237
Why would you just scrape it off
without thinking?!

17:10.320 --> 17:11.864
The seal is obviously suspicious!

17:11.947 --> 17:14.491
I thought it might be because of this!

17:14.575 --> 17:16.118
Everyone, look up!

17:16.201 --> 17:17.703
You can see the sky!

17:18.203 --> 17:20.581
Maybe we can get out from there--

17:20.664 --> 17:21.832
Get down!

17:28.589 --> 17:29.506
Ago...

17:31.592 --> 17:33.218
What should I do?

17:33.302 --> 17:34.928
Right now...

17:35.012 --> 17:37.181
I'm not wearing my sylph shoes.

17:49.943 --> 17:51.278
Master!

17:51.361 --> 17:52.946
A dragon, huh?

17:53.447 --> 17:54.782
Master, so--

17:54.865 --> 17:56.617
Here it comes. Hold on.

18:06.001 --> 18:08.378
I'm letting go. Hold on tight.

18:08.462 --> 18:09.463
Okay!

19:07.396 --> 19:11.066
It's okay now. Seems like it passed out.

19:12.568 --> 19:13.402
Agott?

19:13.485 --> 19:14.653
Oh! Uh...

19:14.736 --> 19:17.156
- Um, right.
- Master!

19:17.239 --> 19:19.074
Tetia and Richeh.

19:19.575 --> 19:21.702
How did you get here, Master?

19:21.785 --> 19:23.328
I was looking for you

19:23.412 --> 19:25.622
when the space suddenly opened...

19:28.667 --> 19:29.668
Where's Coco?

19:35.591 --> 19:37.092
Hello, Coco.

19:38.010 --> 19:39.845
It's been a long wait

19:40.637 --> 19:43.765
for the seed I planted to finally sprout.

19:44.933 --> 19:48.270
How was the task I prepared for you?

19:48.896 --> 19:51.398
Did it help you grow?

19:52.065 --> 19:55.611
I know. I'll give you a gift.

19:56.361 --> 19:58.947
Something you won't learn from Qifrey.

19:59.031 --> 20:01.116
I'll be the one to teach you.

20:01.742 --> 20:03.368
When the time comes, you'll...

20:04.203 --> 20:07.873
Ah, I'm looking forward to that day.

20:19.885 --> 20:21.803
Master Qifrey?

20:22.429 --> 20:23.639
Everyone...

20:27.309 --> 20:29.102
- Agott!
- I'm here.

20:29.811 --> 20:31.813
Thank you for this, Tartah.

20:32.314 --> 20:33.440
Yeah, sure.

20:33.941 --> 20:35.692
Then let me go get Gramps...

20:35.776 --> 20:36.944
Thank goodness.

20:37.444 --> 20:40.113
Wait, are we in Kalhn?

20:40.197 --> 20:43.283
Yeah, we all made it back!

20:43.367 --> 20:44.993
I'm glad I found you.

20:45.077 --> 20:47.287
You were collapsed on the tower stairs.

20:47.788 --> 20:49.081
The stairs?

20:50.916 --> 20:53.252
Wait, did the Brimmed Cap
do something to you?

20:53.335 --> 20:54.544
No!

20:54.628 --> 20:58.257
I was just a bit dazed, um...

21:06.723 --> 21:07.891
Are you okay?

21:10.727 --> 21:13.313
I'm fine... Just fine...

21:25.742 --> 21:27.953
I'm... sorry.

21:30.789 --> 21:32.291
It's my fault.

21:32.791 --> 21:34.126
I involved you...

21:35.794 --> 21:36.920
I'm really...

21:38.755 --> 21:40.007
sorry.

21:44.761 --> 21:46.221
I heard from Tetia

21:46.847 --> 21:48.682
about what happened over there.

21:49.433 --> 21:52.185
What you all did there.

21:55.188 --> 21:57.774
And how everyone was saved
thanks to you.

21:57.858 --> 21:59.067
What?

21:59.901 --> 22:02.070
Ideas, just like penwork,

22:02.154 --> 22:04.406
are at the heart of magic.

22:04.489 --> 22:06.825
So let's keep nurturing that
from now on.

22:20.505 --> 22:21.590
Yes!

22:22.966 --> 22:26.136
Coco, I'm so glad you're okay!

22:26.219 --> 22:29.222
I'm sorry I worried you.
You too, Richeh and Agott.

22:29.306 --> 22:30.932
Well, well!

22:31.016 --> 22:33.477
You seem more than fine. Lively, in fact.

22:33.560 --> 22:35.270
Yes, thanks to you.

22:35.771 --> 22:37.731
It's already late.

22:37.814 --> 22:40.067
How about staying at an inn tonight--

22:40.150 --> 22:41.693
- Mr. Nolnoa.
- Hmm?

22:41.777 --> 22:43.737
I have an important request.

22:43.820 --> 22:44.696
Oh?

22:45.405 --> 22:47.949
The seal drawn under this tile.

22:48.492 --> 22:53.372
I'd like you to examine what additives
were mixed into the conjuring ink.

22:53.914 --> 22:56.583
Hmm, additives?

22:56.666 --> 22:58.001
And please,

22:58.085 --> 23:00.587
don't report what happened today
to the Knights Moralis.

23:00.670 --> 23:03.715
What?! But if you see forbidden magic,

23:03.799 --> 23:05.842
you're required to report it.

23:07.928 --> 23:09.429
Don't tell anyone.

23:10.597 --> 23:11.598
Not anyone.

23:22.484 --> 23:23.610
Honestly,

23:23.693 --> 23:25.904
what is going on here?

23:28.490 --> 23:29.616
No.

23:30.325 --> 23:32.119
More like,

23:32.202 --> 23:33.412
what's going to happen?

23:33.954 --> 23:35.872
Subtitle Translation by: Emily Noguchi

23:36.790 --> 23:40.877
EPISODE 6: A GLOW IN THE RAIN
